WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.430
For Avengers: Infinity War, the Russo brothers
managed to successfully juggle a jam-packed,

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.760
star-studded cast of characters without overwhelming
anybody in the process.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.640
That being said, Infinity War did leave a
few characters sidelined.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:18.000
Some such as Ant-Man and Hawkeye were completely
absent, while others made only relatively

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.220
brief appearances.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.660
The Hulk fell into the latter category.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.460
And while the big guy was mostly overshadowed
by his alter ego Bruce Banner after his early

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.680
defeat at Thanos’ hands, he surely won’t
be out of action for much longer.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:31.840
Here’s why.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.480
"And Hulk… smash.”

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.320
Inner demons

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.000
The Hulk we saw in Infinity War was clearly
struggling with his inner demons not least

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.380
the shame of his initial encounter with Thanos.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.020
“Dude, you’re embarrassing me in front
of the wizards.”

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.260
As it turns out, however, there’s actually
a lot more going on, too.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:00.030
As co-director Joe Russo explains on the Infinity
War commentary:

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:05.360
“I think ultimately what it is is that he's
tired of playing hero to Bruce Banner/"

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.460
One way or the other, Hulk's unwillingness
to participate in the events of Infinity War

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.540
was a crucial part of both his and Banner’s
character arcs.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.500
This has only been a good thing for the Hulk’s
legacy in the wider MCU: as fascinating as

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:21.630
Banner's struggles can be, the onscreen Hulk
has been a little too one-dimensional character

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.780
for a little too long.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:26.780
This twist should bring some new depth to
a character who, for many, is regarded as

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.070
little more than a big, green wrecking ball.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:34.080
And Avengers 4 is as good a chance as any
to solidify Hulk’s legacy as a three-dimensional

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:34.580
character.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.380
Jekyll meets Hyde

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.939
In 2018, Mark Ruffalo hinted at a rocky future
for the relationship between Bruce Banner

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:42.440
and the Hulk.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.760
“And the only one banner probably dislikes
more than anything else is Hulk.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.400
And, they're they’re heading for a showdown.”

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.020
That showdown he mentions never really occurred
in Infinity War, leaving the door wide open

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.080
for these warring personalities to clash in
Avengers 4.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.620
Between Ruffalo's remarks about a Hulk/Banner
showdown and the Russos’ statements about

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:06.550
Hulk getting tired of bailing out Banner,
Avengers 4 could even be the point at which

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:11.249
the MCU gets its first taste of Professor
Hulk a character created in the comics when

00:02:11.249 --> 00:02:16.620
Hulk and Banner united into a single personality,
combining the latter’s brains and the former’s

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.120
brawn.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:22.599
Avengers 4 concept art leaked in 2018, depicting
the Hulk in an Avengers team outfit, would

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.200
seem to back up this possibility.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.060
Running the gauntlet

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.540
Some fans have suggested that, in Avengers
4, Tony Stark will end up going back in time

00:02:31.549 --> 00:02:35.969
gathering up past versions of the Infinity
Stones along the way in order to build his

00:02:35.969 --> 00:02:37.220
own Infinity Gauntlet.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.500
And if he succeeds, it stands to reason that
somebody with a fair amount of heft is going

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.480
to be needed to wield it once it's made.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.800
The idea that this Gauntlet-slinging giant
could be Hulk becomes even more appealing

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.600
when you take a Professor Hulk scenario into
consideration.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:55.719
If the Hulk and Banner do join forces and
don an Infinity Gauntlet, it's hard to imagine

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:59.540
that it wouldn't be a powerful enough combo
to put Thanos out of action once and for all.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.120
A one-sided fight

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.180
Another Avengers 4 rumor posits that, at some
point during the movie, the Hulk will end

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.180
up losing an arm.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.260
But, let’s be completely honest here — it’s
not like he’d be the first.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.060
“Do I look like Iron Man?

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:12.660
Stark is…"

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.900
“I’m sorry - I, oh.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.480
I’m sure that’s going to be okay.”

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:23.020
So what could possibly happen that would lead
to Earth’s greenest hero losing his arm?

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.880
Three words: Stark's Infinity Gauntlet.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.480
If the Hulk were to take on Thanos gauntlet
against gauntlet it would stand to reason

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:34.579
that the only way to win would be the removal
of the opponent's gauntlet... by whatever

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.640
means necessary.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.089
Take all these pieces and put them together,
and you get a picture of Banner and Hulk uniting

00:03:40.089 --> 00:03:44.409
into Professor Hulk, wielding an Infinity
Gauntlet against Thanos and losing an arm

00:03:44.409 --> 00:03:45.120
in the process.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.580
Wild conjecture?

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:51.580
You bet but then again, so is basically everything
else surrounding Avengers 4 right now.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.260
The story’s end

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.040
We may not know much about what Marvel has
planned for whatever happens after Infinity

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:01.999
War, but we do know that the Hulk's carefully
developed story arc has been one of the most

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.600
compelling and crucial elements of the late-stage
MCU.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:09.840
Mark Ruffalo has made it clear in the past
that we've been watching an entire Hulk story

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.300
taking place throughout Thor: Ragnarok, Avengers:
Infinity War, and Avengers 4.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:19.520
Avengers 4 constitutes the third act in that
arc typically, where the hero faces his fears,

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.820
earns redemption and wins a great victory.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.960
This movie won’t just be the conclusion
of the fight against Thanos and the culmination

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:30.150
of the first chapter of the MCU, but also
the climax of the Hulk’s “unofficial”

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:30.879
trilogy, too.

